<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The damage Dismember's strike deals to the one part it takes hold of
    (Ability_Dismember.Strike.cs has the call and the amount). A def of its own so the lost part
    reads "Torn off" and a beheading has its own death message, and so nothing else about a
    vanilla damage type comes along.

    Modeled on Core's Scratch: the Scratch injury is what gives a missing part the "Torn
    off" label, and Crack gives a solid part, a mechanoid's limb, "Shattered". A limb the
    strike could not tear off carries the same injury as a wound, a scratch as deep as the
    strike's damage. The worker is the plain DamageWorker_AddInjury, since Scratch's own
    splits its damage over two parts.
    No armorCategory: the strike ignores armor, so there is no armor stat for it to read,
    and Combat Extended's armor step returns at once for a def without one.
    externalViolence is what makes the target's faction, guilt and the damage records treat
    it as an attack.
  -->
  <DamageDef>
    <defName>HPWC_Dismember</defName>
    <label>dismemberment</label>
    <workerClass>DamageWorker_AddInjury</workerClass>
    <externalViolence>true</externalViolence>
    <deathMessage>{0} has been torn apart.</deathMessage>
    <hediff>Scratch</hediff>
    <hediffSolid>Crack</hediffSolid>
    <impactSoundType>Slice</impactSoundType>
  </DamageDef>
</Defs>
